WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.500
[tense music playing]

2
00:00:12.208 --> 00:00:15.166
[distant shouting]

3
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.250
[dramatic music playing]

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.500
[distant shouting continues]

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

6
00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:47.208
[Úrsula] Now no one will convince them
that this wasn't a miracle.

7
00:00:47.791 --> 00:00:48.875
[sighs]

8
00:00:56.291 --> 00:00:57.750
[Aureliano exhales sharply]

9
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.208
He's awake.

10
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:36.541
[ominous music playing]

11
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:41.166
This is my masterpiece.

12
00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:44.541
This was the only place
where the bullet could get through

13
00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:46.833
without hitting any vital organs.

14
00:01:47.416 --> 00:01:48.791
[Aureliano] What are you saying?

15
00:01:52.166 --> 00:01:54.500
If I still had some authority.

16
00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:57.583
I'd have you executed without trial.

17
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:02.041
Not for saving my life.
but for making me look like a fool.

18
00:02:02.125 --> 00:02:03.125
you son of a bitch.

19
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:06.125
- What are you doing. Aureliano? Enough!
- [doctor] I don't regret what I did.

20
00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:08.208
[Úrsula] Let go. Have you lost your mind?

21
00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:10.791
[doctor] Don't worry. It's all right.

22
00:02:11.458 --> 00:02:13.791
He'll be okay. Excuse me.

23
00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:15.416
[Aureliano groans]

24
00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:18.125
[dramatic ethereal music playing]

25
00:02:28.916 --> 00:02:34.750
ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE

26
00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:36.833
[lively music playing]

27
00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:38.708
[fireworks explode]

28
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:49.083
Ladies and gentlemen. quiet down.

29
00:02:49.166 --> 00:02:51.291
All right. Now let's see what you've got.

30
00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:53.875
It's time to select the winner
of the raffle.

31
00:02:53.958 --> 00:02:57.416
- [man] Maybe I'll win that accordion.
- And the winner of the accordion is…

32
00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.500
[whistling. cheering]

33
00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:00.750
[man 2] Yeah. right. This is rigged!

34
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:03.875
Come on. Show us the paper!
Show us the paper!

35
00:03:03.958 --> 00:03:06.666
- José Arcadio Buendía!
- [man 2] Let's see it. let's see it!

36
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.833
[man 3] All right. all right. bravo!

37
00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:10.541
José Arcadio!

38
00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:14.458
Hey. José Arcadio! I said you won!

39
00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:15.833
Hey!

40
00:03:15.916 --> 00:03:17.708
[narrator] <i>After two whole weeks.</i>

41
00:03:17.791 --> 00:03:20.750
<i>Aureliano Segundo still hadn't told Petra</i>

42
00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:24.541
<i>that she had been sleeping</i>
<i>with both him and his brother.</i>

43
00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:26.250
<i>believing them to be the same man.</i>

44
00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:27.750
Do you like it?

45
00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:29.125
Not more than I like you.

46
00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:31.833
[narrator] <i>And instead of</i>
<i>setting things straight.</i>

47
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.916
<i>he only prolonged the situation.</i>

48
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.000
[lively music continues]

49
00:03:41.541 --> 00:03:43.125
[pensive music playing]

50
00:03:43.208 --> 00:03:45.208
[insects chittering]

51
00:03:50.708 --> 00:03:53.916
[narrator] <i>Meanwhile.</i>
<i>José Arcadio Segundo.</i>

52
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.041
<i>who had not shown any sign of imagination.</i>

53
00:03:58.125 --> 00:04:01.791
<i>was taken over</i>
<i>by the spirit of his great-grandfather.</i>

54
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.625
José Arcadio.

55
00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:07.791
I'm busy.

56
00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:09.333
Have you seen your brother?

57
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.750
He might be asleep still. I don't know.

58
00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:14.291
No. he's not here.

59
00:04:15.791 --> 00:04:17.916
[sighs] You haven't eaten anything.

60
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.375
These flies are having a feast.

61
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.375
Is Great-Grandma in the kitchen?

62
00:04:24.041 --> 00:04:25.000
Yes.

63
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:26.625
Why?

64
00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:32.125
[music fades]

65
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:34.208
[flies buzzing]

66
00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:38.208
Mama Úrsula. can I talk to you?

67
00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.375
What are you up to this time. son?

68
00:04:43.875 --> 00:04:45.708
Do you really have some money saved up?

69
00:04:47.625 --> 00:04:49.125
Who told you that?

70
00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.666
Look. I have an idea.

71
00:04:52.166 --> 00:04:54.000
You better forget about that idea.

72
00:04:54.875 --> 00:04:58.458
- But I haven't even told you what it is.
- There's no need. José Arcadio.

73
00:04:59.041 --> 00:05:01.250
I already know this story by heart.

74
00:05:01.916 --> 00:05:04.291
I recognize that look in your eyes.

75
00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:06.208
and that's enough for me to say no.

76
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.208
[sighs] Mama Úrsula. listen to me.

77
00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:13.541
I've been reading
Great-Grandpa's notes for days.

78
00:05:14.541 --> 00:05:16.500
studying his drawings and inventions.

79
00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:20.041
He was a genius.

80
00:05:21.708 --> 00:05:24.416
Yes. but he was also obsessive

81
00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.083
and couldn't tell where reality ended

82
00:05:27.166 --> 00:05:29.125
and where his madness began.

83
00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:32.750
But have you seen this?

84
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:35.458
[pensive music playing]

85
00:05:35.541 --> 00:05:37.500
Listen to me. José Arcadio.

86
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:39.708
[Úrsula sighs]

87
00:05:40.375 --> 00:05:43.041
The last thing I want
is for you to share his fate.

88
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:45.958
Leave that in the past.

89
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.250
[music fades]

90
00:05:53.375 --> 00:05:55.375
[distant chattering]

91
00:05:56.958 --> 00:05:58.916
[rooster crows]

92
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.000
[insects chittering]

93
00:06:03.666 --> 00:06:05.041
What's the matter with you?

94
00:06:06.333 --> 00:06:09.458
- Mom's worried sick about you.
- Okay. but that's not what I asked you.

95
00:06:11.875 --> 00:06:13.541
You look like you could use a drink.

96
00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:16.791
Come on. let's talk.

97
00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:18.875
[accordion music playing]

98
00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:23.583
Do you know Great-Grandpa
wanted to connect Macondo to the sea?

99
00:06:23.666 --> 00:06:25.916
Ah! Told you those books
were worth checking out.

100
00:06:30.791 --> 00:06:31.916
How about a game?

101
00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:35.416
- Are you even listening?
- Yeah. yeah. but let's have a drink.

102
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.500
My friend. two rums. please.

103
00:06:40.083 --> 00:06:41.208
[men chattering]

104
00:06:44.375 --> 00:06:46.666
Why isn't the river fit for navigation?

105
00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:49.291
- [Aureliano II] Who knows?
- [José Arcadio II] River is right there.

106
00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:52.500
I don't understand why
nobody would follow Great-Grandpa's ideas.

107
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.500
Let's go to Catarino's.

108
00:06:56.583 --> 00:06:57.875
Are you all right?

109
00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:03.375
[José Arcadio II]
Imagine what could reach Macondo.

110
00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.750
You aren't even listening. are you?

111
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.375
Yeah. José Arcadio. I am.

112
00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:11.250
Imagine if we could get to the capital
but do it way faster.

113
00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:14.083
I'm talking about actual progress.

114
00:07:17.333 --> 00:07:21.041
If we had a port. we'd have boats.
canoes. ships would dock…

115
00:07:21.125 --> 00:07:23.083
If we had those.
we'd have the whole world.

116
00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:27.166
- [Aureliano II] The world?
- Tourists. businessmen. ideas.

117
00:07:27.666 --> 00:07:29.958
Weren't you the one saying
nothing ever happens around here?

118
00:07:31.791 --> 00:07:32.916
[music fades]

119
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.625
Listen. you can count on me for anything.

120
00:07:35.708 --> 00:07:37.125
And don't worry about Great-Grandma

121
00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:40.958
because. even if we have to lay
every stone ourselves. then we will.

122
00:07:45.208 --> 00:07:47.208
[tense ethereal music playing]

123
00:08:05.166 --> 00:08:06.791
[groans]

124
00:08:10.083 --> 00:08:12.791
[groaning]

125
00:08:14.625 --> 00:08:16.958
[breathes deeply]

126
00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:21.916
[crowd clamoring]

127
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.208
[man] Long live Colonel Buendía!

128
00:08:24.291 --> 00:08:26.500
[crowd] Long live the colonel!

129
00:08:28.916 --> 00:08:30.208
[Úrsula] All right. boys.

130
00:08:30.291 --> 00:08:33.500
Let's put some sweat into it
because we haven't earned our keep yet.

131
00:08:34.208 --> 00:08:35.708
- [Aureliano grunts]
- [man] Here. right?

132
00:08:35.791 --> 00:08:37.916
[Úrsula] Lazy people aren't welcome
in this house.

133
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.583
- Take that over there. Put it in the back.
- [man] Bring me that.

134
00:08:40.666 --> 00:08:42.708
- Yes. ma'am.
- And you. pick up all those dead leaves.

135
00:08:42.791 --> 00:08:44.875
Look! This whole area is a complete mess.

136
00:08:44.958 --> 00:08:48.083
Ah. that's perfect.
That can go behind the tree.

137
00:08:48.166 --> 00:08:49.375
[Aureliano grunts]

138
00:08:49.958 --> 00:08:51.416
Stop right there. Mr. Buendía.

139
00:08:51.916 --> 00:08:53.750
Who are you.
and what are you doing in my house?

140
00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.125
Allow me to explain. sir.

141
00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:57.708
The president sent our troop here
to protect you.

142
00:08:57.791 --> 00:08:59.000
and it's best to be discreet.

143
00:08:59.083 --> 00:09:01.666
- What are you talking about?
- It's not safe for you to leave.

144
00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.541
[Úrsula] These all need to be watered.

145
00:09:03.625 --> 00:09:05.625
[indistinct chattering in distance]

146
00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.708
You're not well enough yet.

147
00:09:09.791 --> 00:09:11.791
Go and lay down. Aureliano.

148
00:09:11.875 --> 00:09:13.541
Either you get 'em out of here. or I will.

149
00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:17.166
- What's the matter? What is it?
- I said get the hell out of here!

150
00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:20.041
What in the world has gotten into you?

151
00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:22.875
What's it to you
if I put these boys to work?

152
00:09:22.958 --> 00:09:26.375
You think I'm going to waste the only help
the government's ever sent to us?

153
00:09:27.083 --> 00:09:28.541
Are you insane?

154
00:09:29.208 --> 00:09:32.333
You are way too old
to believe in those fairy tales.

155
00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:38.208
Martínez. go fetch the clothes
I left on the clothes line.

156
00:09:41.041 --> 00:09:42.541
What are you waiting for?

157
00:09:45.708 --> 00:09:47.041
Get back to work!

158
00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:49.583
Quit gossiping!
The yard won't clean itself!

159
00:09:49.666 --> 00:09:52.416
- [man] All right. soldiers. You heard her.
- Look. I'm warning you.

160
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.333
[Úrsula] Enough with this nonsense.
Pull yourself together.

161
00:09:55.416 --> 00:09:57.041
You are too old to be acting like this.

162
00:09:57.125 --> 00:09:58.375
I said I'm warning you.

163
00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:01.291
Save your breath.
Get it together. Aureliano.

164
00:10:03.041 --> 00:10:05.000
Talk to her like that again.
I swear I'll kill you.

165
00:10:05.083 --> 00:10:06.166
Shut up. José Arcadio.

166
00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.250
You couldn't kill a fly
if your life depended on it.

167
00:10:08.333 --> 00:10:10.000
you pathetic little bastard!

168
00:10:10.083 --> 00:10:12.208
[man] Come on.
We have to get this done quickly.

169
00:10:15.458 --> 00:10:19.041
[indistinct chanting in distance]

170
00:10:23.291 --> 00:10:24.333
Who are you?

171
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:25.916
Martínez.

172
00:10:27.708 --> 00:10:30.250
If you get mud on those sheets.
Mama Úrsula will kill you.

173
00:10:32.375 --> 00:10:33.916
Hold it up. I'll help you clean it.

174
00:10:37.625 --> 00:10:39.166
Here. like this. Hold it.

175
00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:42.291
And dust it off like this.

176
00:10:42.916 --> 00:10:44.000
Brush it off.

177
00:10:44.875 --> 00:10:45.875
Give me a hand.

178
00:10:49.083 --> 00:10:50.791
[Aureliano] You think this is a joke?

179
00:10:54.583 --> 00:10:55.583
Get out.

180
00:10:56.291 --> 00:10:57.416
Get out!

181
00:10:57.916 --> 00:10:59.666
[man] Everyone out! Let's go!

182
00:11:00.666 --> 00:11:02.833
- Move out! Come on!
- [crowd] Viva!

183
00:11:02.916 --> 00:11:04.541
[groans] You better run.

184
00:11:05.708 --> 00:11:07.375
And take those screaming lunatics
with you!

185
00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:09.208
I want them far away from my house!

186
00:11:09.291 --> 00:11:12.333
[crowd shouting in distance]

187
00:11:12.416 --> 00:11:14.041
We're gonna break through those.

188
00:11:14.666 --> 00:11:16.000
It's not gonna be easy.

189
00:11:17.125 --> 00:11:18.208
[man] You got it.

190
00:11:19.583 --> 00:11:22.375
If a Buendía can't break those rocks.
nobody can.

191
00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:24.333
- [man] You sound like your grandpa.
- He's worse.

192
00:11:24.416 --> 00:11:27.041
[narrator] <i>In an unexpected burst</i>
<i>of audacity.</i>

193
00:11:27.541 --> 00:11:31.291
<i>José Arcadio recruited a group of men.</i>
<i>gathered some tools.</i>

194
00:11:31.375 --> 00:11:34.041
<i>and set out on a colossal undertaking.</i>

195
00:11:34.125 --> 00:11:38.583
<i>determined to break stones.</i>
<i>dig canals. and even level waterfalls.</i>

196
00:11:38.666 --> 00:11:39.958
- I got it. I got it.
- Pull. pull!

197
00:11:40.041 --> 00:11:41.958
- Just like that. come on.
- [man] We got it.

198
00:11:42.041 --> 00:11:43.958
[narrator] <i>It was an impossible dream.</i>

199
00:11:44.041 --> 00:11:47.083
<i>comparable only to those</i>
<i>of his great-grandfather.</i>

200
00:11:47.166 --> 00:11:50.166
[man 2] Come on now!
It's not gonna work. It's stuck.

201
00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.791
I'll get it. Here. hold this.

202
00:11:55.458 --> 00:11:57.583
[man 1] That's it. Keep pulling.
Stack it on the others.

203
00:11:57.666 --> 00:11:59.291
[man 2] All right. all right. you ready?

204
00:11:59.375 --> 00:12:01.250
[accordion music playing]

205
00:12:01.333 --> 00:12:02.375
Let's go. let's go.

206
00:12:05.041 --> 00:12:08.000
[narrator] <i>And while his brother</i>
<i>worked tirelessly.</i>

207
00:12:08.666 --> 00:12:12.500
<i>Aureliano Segundo worked</i>
<i>on cultivating laziness.</i>

208
00:12:12.583 --> 00:12:16.583
<i>indulging in endless parties</i>
<i>at Petra Cotes' house.</i>

209
00:12:17.583 --> 00:12:18.541
Petra!

210
00:12:27.833 --> 00:12:29.625
Welcome. Come in.

211
00:12:29.708 --> 00:12:31.541
Go on. Go right in.

212
00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:33.166
How are you doing?

213
00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.250
[accordion music continues]

214
00:12:44.916 --> 00:12:46.166
[music fades]

215
00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:53.791
[narrator] <i>One night.</i>
<i>Aureliano Segundo discovered he was sick.</i>

216
00:12:53.875 --> 00:12:56.250
[agitated breathing]

217
00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:02.041
[narrator] <i>Two days later.</i>
<i>he found his brother soaked in sweat.</i>

218
00:13:02.125 --> 00:13:04.500
<i>tears streaming down his face.</i>

219
00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.583
[agitated groaning]

220
00:13:06.666 --> 00:13:10.375
[narrator] <i>José Arcadio told his brother</i>
<i>that Petra had rejected him</i>

221
00:13:10.458 --> 00:13:12.875
<i>for giving her a filthy disease.</i>

222
00:13:15.875 --> 00:13:17.333
[Petra] Disgusting pig!

223
00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.208
Who cares. anyway?

224
00:13:20.291 --> 00:13:21.750
There's better ones than her.

225
00:13:26.458 --> 00:13:28.541
I wouldn't be so sure. José Arcadio.

226
00:13:33.041 --> 00:13:35.041
Don't take it out on Petra.
She doesn't know.

227
00:13:38.208 --> 00:13:39.958
I tricked you guys. [chuckles]

228
00:13:43.083 --> 00:13:44.375
See that accordion?

229
00:13:45.416 --> 00:13:47.583
I won it at Petra's house.
using your name.

230
00:13:47.666 --> 00:13:49.291
Oh. when you were drunk at Catarino's…

231
00:13:49.791 --> 00:13:52.500
- Where'd you think I was?
- You're such a scumbag.

232
00:13:52.583 --> 00:13:53.875
[laughs]

233
00:13:54.958 --> 00:13:56.250
No. no! Hey. don't!

234
00:13:57.416 --> 00:13:59.375
Who needs enemies with brothers like us?

235
00:13:59.875 --> 00:14:02.583
- Who's gonna knock?
- You. Aureliano.

236
00:14:06.416 --> 00:14:07.458
[Petra] Who is it?

237
00:14:08.833 --> 00:14:09.791
José Arcadio.

238
00:14:09.875 --> 00:14:11.541
[José Arcadio II] Oh fuck. Here we go.

239
00:14:11.625 --> 00:14:13.500
[Petra] I told you
I didn't wanna see you again.

240
00:14:13.583 --> 00:14:15.708
[Aurelian II] No. you didn't tell me.

241
00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.875
You told him.

242
00:14:24.458 --> 00:14:25.583
I'm Aureliano. Petra.

243
00:14:25.666 --> 00:14:28.041
You confused me for my brother.
I confused you for my brother.

244
00:14:28.125 --> 00:14:30.083
We were all confused.
but we don't mind sharing.

245
00:14:30.166 --> 00:14:32.541
- I mean. my brother thought he was me so…
- [Petra] Hold on.

246
00:14:33.208 --> 00:14:34.500
What's your name again?

247
00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:38.208
- Aureliano.
- Oh. really?

248
00:14:38.291 --> 00:14:40.791
Why don't you go sleep with him. then.
if you don't mind sharing?

249
00:14:40.875 --> 00:14:44.333
Or in other words. go fuck yourself.
José Arcadio. José… Whoever you are.

250
00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.208
Now leave me the hell alone!

251
00:14:59.208 --> 00:15:01.458
[Remedios the Beauty]
Is it true you never had a boyfriend?

252
00:15:02.083 --> 00:15:04.208
Well. it wasn't for a lack of suitors.

253
00:15:09.166 --> 00:15:10.583
So then it is true.

254
00:15:11.625 --> 00:15:12.708
You're a virgin.

255
00:15:12.791 --> 00:15:14.041
[sewing machine stops]

256
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.000
[sewing machine resumes]

257
00:15:32.541 --> 00:15:34.833
[sensual percussive music playing]

258
00:15:34.916 --> 00:15:36.291
What are you doing here?

259
00:15:38.208 --> 00:15:40.333
The colonel will kill you if he finds out.

260
00:15:40.416 --> 00:15:43.250
Mrs. Buendía wants you to show me
where you keep the salt.

261
00:16:02.875 --> 00:16:04.041
This is the salt.

262
00:16:04.791 --> 00:16:06.375
Remedios. I…

263
00:16:06.875 --> 00:16:08.041
What's the matter?

264
00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:11.625
I feel like my heart might explode.

265
00:16:20.625 --> 00:16:22.625
[heart pounding rapidly]

266
00:16:25.541 --> 00:16:26.833
It sounds fine to me.

267
00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.833
You don't understand. Remedios.

268
00:16:32.791 --> 00:16:34.166
I'm dying for you. you see?

269
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.708
Please don't leave me like this.

270
00:16:37.791 --> 00:16:39.208
[somber tense music playing]

271
00:16:40.083 --> 00:16:42.458
[grunts. groans]

272
00:16:42.541 --> 00:16:44.541
[breathing heavily]

273
00:16:46.833 --> 00:16:47.750
Remedios…

274
00:16:49.875 --> 00:16:50.791
Reme…

275
00:17:00.166 --> 00:17:02.166
[somber tense music continues]

276
00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:08.333
Smile. Remedios.

277
00:17:09.291 --> 00:17:11.875
You've officially killed
your first Conservative.

278
00:17:13.458 --> 00:17:15.208
For the love of God. Aureliano.

279
00:17:15.291 --> 00:17:17.291
That's a human being you're talking about.

280
00:17:18.583 --> 00:17:20.625
[Remedios the Beauty]
A very simple one. Mama Úrsula.

281
00:17:20.708 --> 00:17:23.291
He said he was dying for me
like I'm some awful plague.

282
00:17:23.791 --> 00:17:24.791
[Aureliano] You see?

283
00:17:26.083 --> 00:17:28.541
Don't let anybody tell you otherwise.
young lady.

284
00:17:29.083 --> 00:17:31.250
You are the brightest of the Buendías.

285
00:17:35.541 --> 00:17:37.750
[Úrsula] That girl
is gonna give me a heart attack.

286
00:17:43.625 --> 00:17:46.500
[Gerineldo] Since you probably
haven't heard anything. I have news.

287
00:17:46.583 --> 00:17:47.875
[somber ethereal music playing]

288
00:17:47.958 --> 00:17:51.000
The president's acting in violation
of the treaty you signed.

289
00:17:54.708 --> 00:17:56.041
What does it say?

290
00:17:56.125 --> 00:17:58.583
Well. among other bullshit.

291
00:17:58.666 --> 00:18:02.833
it says the president will not reward
former soldiers with war pensions.

292
00:18:02.916 --> 00:18:06.583
regardless of whether they are
Liberal or Conservative.

293
00:18:06.666 --> 00:18:08.458
So they've stabbed us in the back.

294
00:18:09.708 --> 00:18:12.375
Our soldiers will be old men
before they see a cent.

295
00:18:12.458 --> 00:18:13.708
Aureliano…

296
00:18:16.625 --> 00:18:18.666
Did you ever really trust them?

297
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.166
We have to respond immediately.

298
00:18:23.791 --> 00:18:27.666
Well. that's not the only news I bring.

299
00:18:29.666 --> 00:18:34.291
Next month. the president himself
will be visiting Macondo.

300
00:18:34.375 --> 00:18:36.375
He wants to give you a medal
for your participation

301
00:18:36.458 --> 00:18:37.875
in the peace treaty.

302
00:18:37.958 --> 00:18:41.125
They're even holding a public ceremony
for you at the church.

303
00:18:47.541 --> 00:18:49.541
[melodic accordion music playing]

304
00:18:53.125 --> 00:18:54.666
[distant howl]

305
00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.125
[distant barking]

306
00:18:58.958 --> 00:19:00.958
[barking continues]

307
00:19:23.541 --> 00:19:25.708
[Petra] You think this little act
is gonna work on me?

308
00:19:26.958 --> 00:19:28.750
Tell me what I have to do to fix things.

309
00:19:29.291 --> 00:19:30.750
Or is it that you don't miss me?

310
00:19:31.625 --> 00:19:33.166
'Cause if you don't. then I'll leave.

311
00:19:35.791 --> 00:19:37.458
Come on. Petra. I love you.

312
00:19:38.916 --> 00:19:41.583
What you and I had was real.
and you know that.

313
00:19:46.208 --> 00:19:47.875
So who was the bad lay. then?

314
00:19:47.958 --> 00:19:49.208
You or your brother?

315
00:19:51.125 --> 00:19:52.458
[chuckles]

316
00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.291
Who do you think?

317
00:19:57.333 --> 00:20:00.083
[Petra moaning]

318
00:20:00.166 --> 00:20:01.916
[rooster crows in distance]

319
00:20:05.291 --> 00:20:06.708
Hey. Petra.

320
00:20:06.791 --> 00:20:08.541
- [Petra] Huh?
- Didn't you have two rabbits?

321
00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:10.458
Yeah. why?

322
00:20:11.166 --> 00:20:12.666
Has this happened before?

323
00:20:14.208 --> 00:20:16.250
No. Never.

324
00:20:17.125 --> 00:20:20.333
Do you think my roof would be
full of holes if that were the case?

325
00:20:27.166 --> 00:20:29.083
[lively percussive music playing]

326
00:20:29.166 --> 00:20:30.666
What if this works on cows?

327
00:20:39.208 --> 00:20:41.208
[both laughing]

328
00:20:49.208 --> 00:20:52.416
[indistinct shouting in distance]

329
00:20:56.833 --> 00:20:59.916
[indistinct chattering]

330
00:21:18.875 --> 00:21:21.500
[narrator] <i>Aureliano convinced himself</i>
<i>that Petra's love</i>

331
00:21:21.583 --> 00:21:24.208
<i>had the power to rouse nature.</i>

332
00:21:26.041 --> 00:21:27.375
[bellowing]

333
00:21:27.458 --> 00:21:29.583
[bleating]

334
00:21:29.666 --> 00:21:32.208
[clucking]

335
00:21:32.291 --> 00:21:33.666
[whinnying]

336
00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.750
[squealing]

337
00:21:35.833 --> 00:21:37.833
[Petra moaning]

338
00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:51.583
Hey. boss.

339
00:21:52.625 --> 00:21:53.958
Did a nice job here.

340
00:21:54.625 --> 00:21:56.416
[narrator] <i>And without much effort.</i>

341
00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:00.333
<i>he amassed one of the greatest fortunes</i>
<i>in the whole swamp.</i>

342
00:22:01.291 --> 00:22:02.375
[Petra chuckles]

343
00:22:04.625 --> 00:22:06.291
If we're gonna connect Macondo
to the world.

344
00:22:06.375 --> 00:22:08.916
the only way is
if we can somehow dig the river out.

345
00:22:09.416 --> 00:22:10.666
All right. so what do you need?

346
00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:15.333
Fifty men at least. dynamite.
some animals. and money

347
00:22:15.416 --> 00:22:16.833
to motivate the guys.

348
00:22:25.125 --> 00:22:27.125
[men cheering]

349
00:22:28.208 --> 00:22:29.791
[José Arcadio II] We did it. Aureliano.

350
00:22:29.875 --> 00:22:31.000
[men shouting indistinctly]

351
00:22:31.083 --> 00:22:32.916
[José Arcadio II]
We did it. brother. We did it.

352
00:22:34.375 --> 00:22:35.958
I told you. I told you.

353
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:38.458
I told you we could do it.

354
00:22:39.083 --> 00:22:40.000
We did it. guys!

355
00:22:40.083 --> 00:22:43.000
[narrator] <i>Aureliano Segundo</i>
<i>gave his brother the money he needed</i>

356
00:22:43.083 --> 00:22:44.500
<i>for his monumental project.</i>

357
00:22:44.583 --> 00:22:46.375
Send me a telegram if you need more money.

358
00:22:46.458 --> 00:22:47.291
I will.

359
00:22:47.375 --> 00:22:49.791
[narrator] <i>And José Arcadio disappeared</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

360
00:22:49.875 --> 00:22:51.875
[tense music playing]

361
00:22:58.208 --> 00:22:59.625
Aureliano Centeno.

362
00:23:00.416 --> 00:23:03.083
Sir. Aureliano Amador.

363
00:23:03.166 --> 00:23:05.333
My name's Aureliano Arcaya.

364
00:23:05.416 --> 00:23:07.041
Aureliano Triste.

365
00:23:07.125 --> 00:23:09.541
Nice to meet you. Aureliano Serrador.

366
00:23:09.625 --> 00:23:11.833
[narrator] <i>With no plan between them.</i>

367
00:23:11.916 --> 00:23:14.458
<i>and without even knowing one another.</i>

368
00:23:14.541 --> 00:23:19.208
<i>the 17 Aurelianos had come</i>
<i>from the farthest corners of the coast.</i>

369
00:23:19.291 --> 00:23:22.958
<i>drawn by the talk of the ceremony</i>
<i>to honor the colonel.</i>

370
00:23:23.833 --> 00:23:25.833
[bell ringing]

371
00:23:38.666 --> 00:23:39.541
Who are they?

372
00:23:51.416 --> 00:23:53.708
[military band music playing]

373
00:24:02.375 --> 00:24:03.750
- Mr. Buendía.
- [music stops]

374
00:24:04.791 --> 00:24:07.500
Thank you so much for joining us
and participating in this mass

375
00:24:07.583 --> 00:24:08.791
before the big celebration.

376
00:24:08.875 --> 00:24:11.208
As you know. it's Ash Wednesday. and…

377
00:24:11.291 --> 00:24:13.208
Well. it's an important day for us.

378
00:24:14.125 --> 00:24:15.791
Where is the president?

379
00:24:15.875 --> 00:24:18.625
The president sends
his most heartfelt apologies.

380
00:24:18.708 --> 00:24:22.958
He had to attend to an urgent matter.
but he sent us here on his behalf.

381
00:24:23.666 --> 00:24:25.666
[bell rings]

382
00:24:27.208 --> 00:24:29.208
[tense ethereal music playing]

383
00:24:34.666 --> 00:24:37.458
[Antonio Isabel]
Remember. Aureliano. for you are dust.

384
00:24:38.041 --> 00:24:40.375
and to dust you shall return.

385
00:24:43.291 --> 00:24:45.916
[narrator] <i>More out of amusement</i>
<i>than piety.</i>

386
00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:48.833
<i>they let themselves be led</i>
<i>to the communion rail.</i>

387
00:24:48.916 --> 00:24:52.875
<i>where Father Antonio Isabel</i>
<i>smeared ash on their foreheads.</i>

388
00:24:53.416 --> 00:24:58.541
<i>The colonel endured it. thinking maybe</i>
<i>he had been longing for that afternoon.</i>

389
00:25:05.666 --> 00:25:09.541
I'm not gonna deny it.
For days. I have been anxiously waiting

390
00:25:09.625 --> 00:25:12.000
for our head of state
to come visit our town.

391
00:25:16.375 --> 00:25:18.833
- To put a bullet in his head myself.
- [crowd gasps]

392
00:25:18.916 --> 00:25:20.750
[murmuring]

393
00:25:20.833 --> 00:25:24.208
To make him pay
for the antiquated ways of his regime!

394
00:25:26.125 --> 00:25:29.833
And since he's too busy to be here.
tell him he better follow through

395
00:25:29.916 --> 00:25:32.000
with the pensions
he promised our veterans.

396
00:25:32.083 --> 00:25:33.333
[man] This is ridiculous.

397
00:25:33.416 --> 00:25:37.583
Unless. of course. he'd rather
I gather my old army of soldiers.

398
00:25:37.666 --> 00:25:41.166
And when reunited.
we'll go to war once again!

399
00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:42.708
[crowd gasps. exclaims]

400
00:25:42.791 --> 00:25:44.791
[indistinct chattering]

401
00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:52.083
Take your cheap scrap of metal.

402
00:25:52.166 --> 00:25:54.166
[ominous music playing]

403
00:26:02.166 --> 00:26:04.291
Your men would be really proud of you.

404
00:26:08.625 --> 00:26:11.000
[narrator] <i>The Aurelianos left in a pack.</i>

405
00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:14.833
<i>giving the villagers the impression</i>
<i>that the Buendía bloodline</i>

406
00:26:14.916 --> 00:26:17.250
<i>would take root for centuries to come.</i>

407
00:26:21.458 --> 00:26:22.333
See you.

408
00:26:28.625 --> 00:26:32.250
[narrator] <i>The only one who stayed behind</i>
<i>was Aureliano Triste.</i>

409
00:26:32.333 --> 00:26:37.125
<i>Who. when he went to wipe his forehead.</i>
<i>realized the stain was permanent.</i>

410
00:26:37.208 --> 00:26:38.500
<i>as were his brothers'.</i>

411
00:26:38.583 --> 00:26:40.583
[bell ringing]

412
00:26:40.666 --> 00:26:43.041
[women praying]

413
00:26:44.041 --> 00:26:46.041
[praying continues]

414
00:26:51.291 --> 00:26:53.291
[bell continues ringing]

415
00:27:03.916 --> 00:27:07.083
Hail Mary. full of grace.
the Lord is with thee.

416
00:27:07.166 --> 00:27:09.041
Blessed art thou among women.

417
00:27:09.125 --> 00:27:11.958
and blessed is
the fruit of thy womb. Jesus.

418
00:27:12.041 --> 00:27:13.625
Holy Mary. Mother of God.

419
00:27:13.708 --> 00:27:17.125
pray for us sinners.
now and at the hour of our death.

420
00:27:17.208 --> 00:27:18.250
<i>Amen.</i>

421
00:27:19.416 --> 00:27:21.416
[women praying]

422
00:27:22.166 --> 00:27:23.291
[Mother Superior] Fernanda.

423
00:27:23.375 --> 00:27:25.375
[mysterious music playing]

424
00:27:27.541 --> 00:27:29.166
Please come with me.

425
00:27:45.291 --> 00:27:47.291
[mysterious music continues]

426
00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:24.833
FUNERAL WREATHS FOR SALE

427
00:28:32.291 --> 00:28:33.916
Your mother is upstairs.

428
00:28:34.416 --> 00:28:36.750
But don't bother her
if she's still sleeping.

429
00:29:22.458 --> 00:29:23.916
Why didn't you look for me sooner?

430
00:29:26.875 --> 00:29:27.916
Darling.

431
00:29:29.416 --> 00:29:31.416
[breathing shakily]

432
00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.541
Our family…

433
00:29:35.375 --> 00:29:36.791
Our family

434
00:29:37.750 --> 00:29:41.500
is unfathomably rich
and powerful. darling.

435
00:29:46.500 --> 00:29:50.041
And you'll be queen one day.

436
00:29:50.125 --> 00:29:52.125
[labored breathing]

437
00:29:56.375 --> 00:29:58.375
[music fades]

438
00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:10.666
[José Arcadio II] Over there.
That's where we dock.

439
00:30:11.583 --> 00:30:13.583
[melodic music playing]

440
00:30:15.750 --> 00:30:18.500
[José Arcadio II] Further down.
Keep pulling. guys.

441
00:30:18.583 --> 00:30:21.250
Keep pulling! Just a little further!

442
00:30:23.083 --> 00:30:24.000
Hold!

443
00:30:26.250 --> 00:30:27.791
All right. let's go again!

444
00:30:28.500 --> 00:30:29.916
Come on. boys! Pull!

445
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:30.833
Pull!

446
00:30:33.333 --> 00:30:34.458
[narrator] <i>The news spread</i>

447
00:30:34.541 --> 00:30:37.166
<i>that a strange ship</i>
<i>was approaching the town.</i>

448
00:30:38.791 --> 00:30:41.041
[distant shouting]

449
00:30:46.375 --> 00:30:47.833
[José Arcadio II] We did it!

450
00:30:49.083 --> 00:30:50.875
- Bonjour!
- Bonjour. Macondo!

451
00:30:50.958 --> 00:30:52.916
[men chattering indistinctly]

452
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:54.250
Tie the rope over there.

453
00:30:54.333 --> 00:30:56.125
Right here. right here. Excuse me.

454
00:30:56.208 --> 00:30:59.041
[narrator] <i>It was nothing more</i>
<i>than a raft made of logs.</i>

455
00:30:59.125 --> 00:31:02.875
<i>dragged by 20 men</i>
<i>pulling heavy ropes along the riverbank.</i>

456
00:31:03.750 --> 00:31:05.666
- [indistinct chattering]
- [laughing]

457
00:31:08.666 --> 00:31:10.375
Watch it. Pull us over to your side.

458
00:31:13.041 --> 00:31:14.750
[Aureliano II] I knew he would come.

459
00:31:15.791 --> 00:31:17.083
Are you seeing this. Petra?

460
00:31:17.166 --> 00:31:19.958
- [man] Welcome! Welcome. everyone!
- José Arcadio!

461
00:31:20.583 --> 00:31:22.500
Aureliano!

462
00:31:23.333 --> 00:31:25.000
Guys. give 'em a hand. Give 'em a hand.

463
00:31:31.083 --> 00:31:32.916
Isn't that my friend José Arcadio?

464
00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:36.416
That's José Arcadio.
but not the one you're thinking of.

465
00:31:36.916 --> 00:31:38.166
[lively music playing]

466
00:31:38.250 --> 00:31:39.958
[man 2] Pull! Come on. guys!

467
00:31:40.583 --> 00:31:42.791
[Aureliano II] Everyone said
you had stolen my money.

468
00:31:42.875 --> 00:31:44.333
I told them to go to hell.

469
00:31:46.583 --> 00:31:49.000
- Thank you. Brother. Thank you.
- [woman] Bonjour! Bonjour!

470
00:31:50.291 --> 00:31:51.458
[woman 2] Welcome.

471
00:31:56.291 --> 00:31:57.750
[José Arcadio II] Welcome to Macondo.

472
00:32:03.625 --> 00:32:05.708
[Aureliano II] Let's hear it
for José Arcadio Buendía!

473
00:32:05.791 --> 00:32:07.833
- [all] Buendía!
- [Aureliano II] Yeah!

474
00:32:09.708 --> 00:32:10.750
[all clapping]

475
00:32:10.833 --> 00:32:12.458
- And for Macondo!
- [all cheering]

476
00:32:16.041 --> 00:32:18.000
[Aureliano II] You see. Petra? I told you.

477
00:32:30.416 --> 00:32:31.500
[music fades]

478
00:32:31.583 --> 00:32:34.083
[narrator] <i>That was</i>
<i>the first and last ship</i>

479
00:32:34.166 --> 00:32:36.041
<i>to ever dock in Macondo.</i>

480
00:32:36.125 --> 00:32:38.500
[triumphant music playing]

481
00:32:39.583 --> 00:32:40.791
[music stops]

482
00:32:43.458 --> 00:32:45.458
[indistinct chattering]

483
00:32:47.708 --> 00:32:48.791
[woman] <i>Et voilà.</i>

484
00:32:48.875 --> 00:32:50.875
[romantic music playing]

485
00:33:04.458 --> 00:33:07.625
[narrator] <i>All that remained</i>
<i>of that unfortunate venture</i>

486
00:33:08.333 --> 00:33:11.833
<i>was the breath of fresh air</i>
<i>brought by the matrons from France.</i>

487
00:33:15.083 --> 00:33:20.000
<i>At first. curiosity lured more clientele</i>
<i>to the forbidden street.</i>

488
00:33:21.166 --> 00:33:24.083
<i>And there were even rumors</i>
<i>that respectable ladies</i>

489
00:33:24.166 --> 00:33:26.458
<i>disguised themselves as working-class men</i>

490
00:33:26.541 --> 00:33:29.666
<i>to see the novelty of the gramophone</i>
<i>up close.</i>

491
00:33:33.208 --> 00:33:35.708
<i>But after observing it so closely.</i>

492
00:33:35.791 --> 00:33:40.041
<i>they came to the conclusion</i>
<i>that it wasn't some magical device.</i>

493
00:33:41.541 --> 00:33:44.500
<i>It was a mechanical trick</i>
<i>that could never compare</i>

494
00:33:44.583 --> 00:33:47.708
<i>to something as moving. as human.</i>

495
00:33:48.208 --> 00:33:51.958
<i>and as alive as a real band of musicians.</i>

496
00:33:52.041 --> 00:33:54.041
[romantic music continues]

497
00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:27.208
[music fades]

498
00:34:31.708 --> 00:34:33.708
[people murmuring]

499
00:34:37.083 --> 00:34:38.916
- [woman 1] Mother of God!
- [man 1] Look at that!

500
00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:40.208
[woman 2] It's beautiful!

501
00:34:40.708 --> 00:34:41.708
[woman 3] Is it magic?

502
00:34:41.791 --> 00:34:42.750
[woman 4] What is it?

503
00:34:44.625 --> 00:34:46.708
[cheerful music playing]

504
00:34:53.291 --> 00:34:55.291
[Petra laughing]

505
00:35:07.666 --> 00:35:11.208
[narrator] <i>Dazzled by so many</i>
<i>and such marvelous inventions.</i>

506
00:35:11.708 --> 00:35:15.750
<i>the people of Macondo didn't know</i>
<i>where to begin in their amazement.</i>

507
00:35:18.375 --> 00:35:19.541
[Sofía] Remedios.

508
00:35:19.625 --> 00:35:21.083
[music fades]

509
00:35:23.875 --> 00:35:28.000
[narrator] <i>They'd stay up at night</i>
<i>admiring the pale electric bulbs.</i>

510
00:35:28.083 --> 00:35:30.208
[melancholy music playing]

511
00:35:37.333 --> 00:35:39.333
[banging at door]

512
00:35:48.791 --> 00:35:49.791
Hello.

513
00:35:49.875 --> 00:35:51.500
Are you here for the funeral wreaths?

514
00:35:51.583 --> 00:35:52.500
[man 1] No.

515
00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:54.958
Good afternoon. miss.
We're looking for a--

516
00:35:55.041 --> 00:35:56.291
[man 2] My apologies. Chavarría.

517
00:35:57.500 --> 00:35:59.166
This is my daughter. Fernanda.

518
00:35:59.666 --> 00:36:00.916
Please. come in.

519
00:36:02.875 --> 00:36:05.500
[narrator] <i>News of the colonel's threat</i>
<i>to the president</i>

520
00:36:05.583 --> 00:36:08.083
<i>had reached far away territories</i>

521
00:36:08.708 --> 00:36:12.625
<i>and raised concern for those</i>
<i>who still considered the Buendía name</i>

522
00:36:12.708 --> 00:36:14.166
<i>a symbol of subversion.</i>

523
00:36:14.250 --> 00:36:15.166
[father] I'm listening.

524
00:36:15.250 --> 00:36:17.458
[man 2] This is your chance
to make yourself indispensable

525
00:36:17.541 --> 00:36:18.541
to the Conservative Party.

526
00:36:18.625 --> 00:36:20.000
[father] At your service. sir.

527
00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:23.000
[mysterious music playing]

528
00:36:36.958 --> 00:36:38.583
Fernanda. get your things ready.

529
00:36:38.666 --> 00:36:40.000
[music fades]

530
00:36:40.083 --> 00:36:41.750
You have a long trip ahead.

531
00:36:55.250 --> 00:36:56.750
[narrator] <i>Convinced by her father</i>

532
00:36:56.833 --> 00:36:59.625
<i>that the day of her coronation</i>
<i>had arrived.</i>

533
00:36:59.708 --> 00:37:04.375
<i>Fernanda set out for the distant kingdom</i>
<i>where she would be queen.</i>

534
00:37:04.458 --> 00:37:06.458
[tense ethereal music playing]

535
00:37:16.541 --> 00:37:18.625
I swear you are not of this world.

536
00:37:22.708 --> 00:37:25.416
[narrator] <i>They pestered</i>
<i>Remedios the Beauty so much</i>

537
00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:27.541
<i>about cutting her abundant hair</i>

538
00:37:27.625 --> 00:37:29.791
<i>that she simply shaved her head.</i>

539
00:37:30.291 --> 00:37:32.666
<i>finally freeing herself from the heat.</i>

540
00:37:32.750 --> 00:37:34.166
Are you going to the carnival?

541
00:37:35.375 --> 00:37:36.666
I don't think so.

542
00:37:44.916 --> 00:37:45.833
Give me that.

543
00:37:52.666 --> 00:37:54.583
Mama Úrsula told me
the only saint in this family

544
00:37:54.666 --> 00:37:55.666
was your wife.

545
00:37:56.625 --> 00:37:58.458
And that's why she gave me her name.

546
00:37:59.041 --> 00:38:00.458
- [Aureliano] Hmm.
- [music fades]

547
00:38:02.750 --> 00:38:03.916
Do I look like her?

548
00:38:07.583 --> 00:38:08.958
I don't know anymore.

549
00:38:09.791 --> 00:38:11.041
But "Remedios."

550
00:38:12.458 --> 00:38:13.750
it's a beautiful name.

551
00:38:14.458 --> 00:38:16.458
[lively mysterious music playing]

552
00:38:17.666 --> 00:38:18.791
It really is.

553
00:38:22.875 --> 00:38:24.875
[percussive music playing]

554
00:38:34.916 --> 00:38:36.916
[music intensifies]

555
00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:39.000
[crowd cheering. shouting]

556
00:38:48.375 --> 00:38:49.750
[laughing]

557
00:38:49.833 --> 00:38:51.833
[howling]

558
00:38:55.666 --> 00:38:56.791
Remedios!

559
00:38:56.875 --> 00:38:58.625
Aureliano!

560
00:39:02.958 --> 00:39:05.166
[man chanting]

561
00:39:19.333 --> 00:39:20.875
[music fades]

562
00:39:25.083 --> 00:39:27.083
[ethereal music playing]

563
00:39:44.958 --> 00:39:46.291
[whistling]

564
00:39:46.375 --> 00:39:48.625
- [lively percussive music playing]
- [cheering]

565
00:39:57.458 --> 00:39:59.458
[cheering continues]

566
00:40:28.375 --> 00:40:29.250
Welcome.

567
00:40:29.875 --> 00:40:31.666
I'm Aureliano Buendía. And you?

568
00:40:35.958 --> 00:40:37.541
Fernanda del Carpio.

569
00:40:40.041 --> 00:40:42.041
[whistle rhythmically blowing]

570
00:40:59.916 --> 00:41:01.916
[whistle rhythmically blowing]

571
00:41:12.708 --> 00:41:13.791
[music stops]

572
00:41:13.875 --> 00:41:14.958
My friends.

573
00:41:16.291 --> 00:41:18.958
A round of applause
for Fernanda del Carpio.

574
00:41:19.500 --> 00:41:20.750
the queen of Madagascar.

575
00:41:20.833 --> 00:41:22.833
[crowd cheering]

576
00:41:25.166 --> 00:41:26.791
[woman] Long live the queen!

577
00:41:26.875 --> 00:41:28.416
[man] All hail the queen!

578
00:41:30.500 --> 00:41:32.375
And for Remedios the Beauty.

579
00:41:32.458 --> 00:41:34.000
our Queen of Macondo.

580
00:41:34.083 --> 00:41:35.916
[crowd cheering]

581
00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:38.291
[whistle blowing]

582
00:41:39.250 --> 00:41:41.125
[Aureliano II]
Let's hear it for the carnival!

583
00:41:41.208 --> 00:41:43.791
- [crowd cheering]
- [lively percussive music playing]

584
00:42:08.958 --> 00:42:11.125
[fireworks whistling]

585
00:42:11.208 --> 00:42:13.041
[fireworks exploding]

586
00:42:22.875 --> 00:42:24.916
Let's hear it for the Liberal Party!

587
00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.000
[crowd cheering]

588
00:42:31.083 --> 00:42:32.416
[gunshot]

589
00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:35.166
Get down!

590
00:42:36.208 --> 00:42:37.083
Get down!

591
00:42:39.125 --> 00:42:40.166
[music stops]

592
00:42:43.250 --> 00:42:44.208
[man grunts]

593
00:42:44.291 --> 00:42:46.291
[dark percussive music playing]

594
00:43:03.791 --> 00:43:04.916
[gunshot]

595
00:43:19.416 --> 00:43:21.166
[ominous music playing]

596
00:43:22.583 --> 00:43:24.375
[muffled cheering]

597
00:43:28.958 --> 00:43:30.375
- [gunshot]
- [grunts]

598
00:43:30.458 --> 00:43:33.041
- [lively percussive music playing]
- [crowd cheering]

599
00:43:36.625 --> 00:43:38.000
Let's go. let's go. let's go!

600
00:43:40.000 --> 00:43:41.333
[gunshot]

601
00:43:50.750 --> 00:43:52.250
[people screaming]

602
00:43:52.333 --> 00:43:54.041
- [gunshots continue]
- [music stops]

603
00:43:58.416 --> 00:44:00.500
- [panicked screaming]
- [gunshots continue]

604
00:44:04.583 --> 00:44:06.333
[Aureliano II] Come on. come on.
We gotta go.

605
00:44:08.166 --> 00:44:10.166
- [gunshots continue]
- [man grunts]

606
00:44:12.375 --> 00:44:14.833
- Oh my God. Remedios.
- We almost got killed. but now we're fine.

607
00:44:14.916 --> 00:44:17.083
What do you mean? What happened?

608
00:44:17.166 --> 00:44:18.458
What happened?

609
00:44:18.541 --> 00:44:20.541
[distant screaming]

610
00:44:24.125 --> 00:44:25.791
Aureliano. what's going on?

611
00:44:26.291 --> 00:44:27.416
Aureliano.

612
00:44:30.916 --> 00:44:32.000
Bring some water.

613
00:44:32.083 --> 00:44:34.083
[panicked breathing]

614
00:44:52.166 --> 00:44:53.166
You're all right.

615
00:44:54.583 --> 00:44:56.583
[breathing slows]

616
00:45:27.541 --> 00:45:28.500
What happened?

617
00:45:30.541 --> 00:45:31.958
You have a pet porcupine?

618
00:45:37.041 --> 00:45:39.000
It's the roses from the wreaths.

619
00:45:40.125 --> 00:45:42.583
Sometimes I forget
there's thorns to remove.

620
00:45:43.500 --> 00:45:44.541
The wreaths?

621
00:45:46.041 --> 00:45:47.750
We make wreaths for funerals.

622
00:45:51.791 --> 00:45:53.083
Where do you make them?

623
00:45:53.166 --> 00:45:54.416
[door slams]

624
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:56.375
What are you doing here?

625
00:45:57.416 --> 00:45:58.375
Who sent you?

626
00:45:58.458 --> 00:45:59.833
[Aureliano II] Hey. hey. calm down.

627
00:46:00.583 --> 00:46:02.041
Shut up. Aureliano.

628
00:46:02.541 --> 00:46:05.791
I'll calm down as soon as
this lady tells me who tried to kill me!

629
00:46:05.875 --> 00:46:07.375
What the hell are you talking about?

630
00:46:07.458 --> 00:46:10.416
She came with the Bedouins.
and they were the ones shooting at us!

631
00:46:10.500 --> 00:46:12.500
The government sent you. didn't they?

632
00:46:12.583 --> 00:46:13.791
Have you lost your mind?

633
00:46:14.291 --> 00:46:16.666
My brother was right.
You think the world revolves around you.

634
00:46:17.291 --> 00:46:19.500
- You're a real man. aren't you?
- Aureliano. that's enough!

635
00:46:19.583 --> 00:46:20.791
Go on. I dare you.

636
00:46:21.958 --> 00:46:23.625
- Back off. asshole.
- What are you gonna do?

637
00:46:27.041 --> 00:46:29.041
[somber music playing]

638
00:46:33.750 --> 00:46:36.000
[narrator] <i>When peace was restored.</i>

639
00:46:36.958 --> 00:46:40.291
<i>not one of the fake Bedouins</i>
<i>was left in town.</i>

640
00:46:40.791 --> 00:46:44.500
<i>And sprawled across the plaza.</i>
<i>dead and wounded alike.</i>

641
00:46:45.416 --> 00:46:46.958
<i>were nine clowns.</i>

642
00:46:47.500 --> 00:46:49.208
<i>four columbines.</i>

643
00:46:49.291 --> 00:46:51.458
<i>17 playing-card kings.</i>

644
00:46:51.541 --> 00:46:52.666
<i>one devil.</i>

645
00:46:53.333 --> 00:46:54.708
<i>three musicians.</i>

646
00:46:54.791 --> 00:46:56.666
<i>two peers of France.</i>

647
00:46:56.750 --> 00:46:59.250
<i>and three Japanese empresses.</i>

648
00:47:29.000 --> 00:47:31.000
[music fades]

649
00:47:33.166 --> 00:47:34.416
Were you spying on me?

650
00:47:36.166 --> 00:47:37.291
[Úrsula] Not at all.

651
00:47:45.791 --> 00:47:46.750
You were right.

652
00:47:47.750 --> 00:47:49.333
The carnival was a disaster.

653
00:47:50.291 --> 00:47:51.750
Please don't lecture me.

654
00:47:53.250 --> 00:47:54.875
[Úrsula] Well. I'm glad you think so

655
00:47:55.958 --> 00:47:58.125
because I'm not here to lecture you.

656
00:48:06.833 --> 00:48:08.625
Go find her. Aureliano.

657
00:48:11.916 --> 00:48:14.083
There's more to life than just partying.

658
00:48:15.041 --> 00:48:17.166
You don't have children with just anyone.

659
00:48:17.250 --> 00:48:19.541
[poignant music playing]

660
00:48:19.625 --> 00:48:21.541
I saw the way you looked at her.

661
00:48:26.500 --> 00:48:28.833
It was like seeing your great-grandfather.

662
00:48:32.291 --> 00:48:33.166
[Úrsula chuckles]

663
00:48:41.333 --> 00:48:42.458
Go on. son.

664
00:48:44.125 --> 00:48:45.041
Go on.

665
00:48:48.291 --> 00:48:51.291
[narrator] <i>The only real clues</i>
<i>that Aureliano Segundo had</i>

666
00:48:51.375 --> 00:48:53.041
<i>when he went to look for her</i>

667
00:48:53.708 --> 00:48:56.041
<i>were her unmistakable moors accent</i>

668
00:48:56.125 --> 00:48:59.208
<i>and her trade</i>
<i>as a weaver of funeral wreaths.</i>

669
00:49:01.958 --> 00:49:04.250
<i>He searched for her mercilessly</i>

670
00:49:04.750 --> 00:49:08.958
<i>with the same courage José Arcadio showed</i>
<i>when he crossed the mountain range…</i>

671
00:49:11.625 --> 00:49:16.666
<i>with the same blind pride with which</i>
<i>the colonel promoted his useless wars…</i>

672
00:49:19.291 --> 00:49:21.125
<i>and with the same tenacity</i>

673
00:49:21.208 --> 00:49:24.375
<i>with which</i>
<i>Úrsula preserved their bloodline.</i>

674
00:49:25.791 --> 00:49:28.916
<i>Aureliano Segundo pursued Fernanda</i>

675
00:49:30.583 --> 00:49:32.958
<i>without a moment's discouragement.</i>

676
00:49:36.333 --> 00:49:41.333
<i>And although he had never seen them</i>
<i>and no one had ever described them to him.</i>

677
00:49:41.416 --> 00:49:46.000
<i>he recognized at once</i>
<i>the walls eaten away by bone salt.</i>

678
00:49:46.958 --> 00:49:50.000
<i>And nailed to the door was the saddest.</i>

679
00:49:50.083 --> 00:49:53.291
<i>most rain-washed cardboard sign.</i>
<i>which read.</i>

680
00:49:53.958 --> 00:49:56.375
<i>"Funeral wreaths for sale."</i>

681
00:50:10.958 --> 00:50:12.958
[music intensifies]

682
00:50:28.166 --> 00:50:29.750
[music fades]

683
00:50:29.833 --> 00:50:31.833
[thunder rumbles]

684
00:50:34.250 --> 00:50:36.250
[thunderclap]

685
00:50:41.833 --> 00:50:43.833
[tense ethereal music playing]

686
00:50:59.708 --> 00:51:01.708
[dark percussive music playing]

687
00:51:57.166 --> 00:51:59.166
[dark ethereal music playing]

688
00:53:31.916 --> 00:53:33.916
[somber ethereal music playing]

689
00:57:11.958 --> 00:57:13.958
[music fades]

690
00:57:15.375 --> 00:57:17.416
[dark percussive music playing]

691
00:58:26.000 --> 00:58:28.875
[music fades]

692
00:58:29.305 --> 00:59:29.495
